msgid "An introduction to a course on practical applications of quantum computing."
msgstr "Isang panimula sa kurso tungkol sa mga praktikal na aplikasyon ng quantum computing."

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduction"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore  */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to practical near-term quantum computing {#introduction-to-practical-near-term-quantum-computing}"
msgstr "Panimula sa praktikal na near-term quantum computing {#introduction-to-practical-near-term-quantum-computing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ever since quantum computers were first proposed more than four decades ago, the question has been: How far could this new approach extend the limits of computation? Theoretical computer science gave us some exciting answers. Quantum computers could factor large integers dramatically faster than the best-known classical methods, speed up unstructured search, and simulate quantum systems more naturally. However, many of these ideas assumed a future large-scale, fault-tolerant quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Mula nang unang imungkahi ang mga quantum computer mahigit apat na dekada na ang nakalipas, ang tanong ay: Hanggang saan kayang palawakin ng bagong pamamaraang ito ang mga limitasyon ng computation? Nagbigay sa atin ang theoretical computer science ng mga kapana-panabik na sagot. Kaya ng mga quantum computer na mag-factor ng malalaking integer nang mas mabilis kaysa sa pinakakilalang classical na pamamaraan, pabilisin ang unstructured search, at mas natural na i-simulate ang mga quantum system. Gayunpaman, marami sa mga ideyang ito ay nag-assume ng isang hinaharap na malakihan at fault-tolerant na quantum computer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The technology hasn't yet reached all of those theoretical goals, but it is improving rapidly. Researchers can now use quantum processors to explore real scientific and industrial problems. In this course, we'll get hands-on experience with some of the most promising applications. We'll estimate low-energy properties of a complex molecular model, simulate the dynamics of a lattice gauge theory, and explore how a financial portfolio problem can be mapped to a quantum computer. We'll also look at newer areas where we've only begun to understand what quantum computers might offer, including quantum machine learning (QML) and quantum approaches to partial differential equations (PDEs).\n"
msgstr "Hindi pa naaabot ng teknolohiya ang lahat ng teoretikal na layuning iyon, pero mabilis itong bumubuti. Magagamit na ngayon ng mga mananaliksik ang mga quantum processor para tuklasin ang mga totoong problemang pang-agham at pang-industriya. Sa kursong ito, magkakaroon tayo ng hands-on na karanasan sa ilan sa mga pinakamapagpapangakong aplikasyon. Tatantyahin natin ang mga low-energy na katangian ng isang komplikadong molecular model, ie-simulate ang dynamics ng isang lattice gauge theory, at tutuklasin kung paano maimamapa ang isang financial portfolio problem sa isang quantum computer. Titingnan din natin ang mga mas bagong larangan kung saan nagsisimula pa lang nating maunawaan ang maaaring ialok ng mga quantum computer, kabilang ang quantum machine learning (QML) at mga quantum na pamamaraan para sa partial differential equations (PDEs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many of the examples in this course are small enough for a classical computer to solve. That's intentional. The goal is to give you tangible experience with the full process of using a quantum computer to address a real-world problem. Some examples represent problems for which quantum advantage might emerge at much larger scales. In other examples, we use a simplified method so that implementation details don't hide the central quantum idea.\n"
msgstr "Marami sa mga halimbawa sa kursong ito ay sapat na maliit para malutas ng isang classical computer. Sinadya iyon. Layunin nitong bigyan ka ng konkretong karanasan sa buong proseso ng paggamit ng quantum computer para tugunan ang isang real-world na problema. Ang ilang halimbawa ay kumakatawan sa mga problemang maaaring magkaroon ng quantum advantage sa mas malalaking sukat. Sa ibang mga halimbawa, gumagamit tayo ng pinasimpleng pamamaraan para hindi matakpan ng mga detalye ng implementasyon ang sentral na quantum na ideya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By the end of the course, you should have an overview of the main quantum applications and an intuition for why quantum computers might be useful in particular areas. You'll encounter common techniques for representing problems on quantum computers, learn how quantum and classical methods work together, and begin to recognize which tools and tradeoffs matter for different kinds of problems.\n"
msgstr "Pagsapit ng katapusan ng kurso, dapat ay mayroon ka nang pangkalahatang-ideya ng mga pangunahing quantum na aplikasyon at intuwisyon kung bakit maaaring maging kapaki-pakinabang ang mga quantum computer sa mga partikular na larangan. Makikilala mo ang mga karaniwang technique sa pagrepresenta ng mga problema sa mga quantum computer, matututunan kung paano nagtutulungan ang mga quantum at classical na pamamaraan, at sisimulan mong kilalanin kung aling mga tool at tradeoff ang mahalaga sa iba't ibang uri ng problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this first lesson, we'll cover some of the fundamental concepts and terminology that help you understand applications of quantum computing at a high level, and give you an overview of the main application areas that the scientific community is actively pursuing.\n"
msgstr "Sa unang lesson na ito, tatalakayin natin ang ilang pangunahing konsepto at terminolohiya na tumutulong sa iyong maunawaan ang mga aplikasyon ng quantum computing sa mataas na antas, at bibigyan ka ng pangkalahatang-ideya ng mga pangunahing larangan ng aplikasyon na aktibong tinutugis ng siyentipikong komunidad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What quantum computers might be useful for {#what-quantum-computers-might-be-useful-for}"
msgstr "Kung saan maaaring maging kapaki-pakinabang ang mga quantum computer {#what-quantum-computers-might-be-useful-for}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum computers are often framed as competitors to classical computers, but a more appropriate way to think about them is as specialized resources within larger classical workflows. The important question, then, is which parts of a computation are especially well suited to quantum hardware. The most intuitive answer comes from problems that are already quantum, such as the behavior of molecules, materials, and quantum fields. A quantum processor can represent and manipulate quantum states directly, while the resources required for a general classical description grow exponentially with the size of the system.\n"
msgstr "Madalas na inilalarawan ang mga quantum computer bilang katunggali ng mga classical computer, pero mas angkop silang isipin bilang mga espesyalisadong resource sa loob ng mas malalaking classical na workflow. Ang mahalagang tanong, kung gayon, ay kung aling mga bahagi ng isang computation ang lalong angkop sa quantum hardware. Ang pinakamadaling sagot ay mula sa mga problemang quantum na mismo, tulad ng pag-uugali ng mga molecule, materyales, at quantum field. Direktang nirerepresenta at minamanipula ng isang quantum processor ang mga quantum state, habang ang mga resource na kailangan para sa pangkalahatang classical na paglalarawan ay lumalaki nang exponential kasabay ng laki ng system.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The case is more subtle for problems with classical inputs and outputs, but there are still good reasons to explore them. Optimization problems are widespread and economically important, so even a modest improvement in solution quality or runtime could be valuable. Quantum algorithms might also offer new ways to explore complicated solution spaces or exploit structure in particular classes of problems. Quantum machine learning has strong theoretical motivation for certain problems with classical inputs, including structured classification and the processing of massive datasets. However, whether these results can translate into practical advantage on real-world classical data remains an open question. Partial differential equations describe many important systems in science, engineering, and finance, and quantum algorithms might improve the scaling of certain high-dimensional simulations and large linear-algebra problems.\n"
msgstr "Mas masalimuot ang kaso para sa mga problemang may classical na input at output, pero may mga magandang dahilan pa rin para tuklasin ang mga ito. Laganap at mahalaga sa ekonomiya ang mga optimization problem, kaya kahit katamtamang pagbuti sa kalidad ng solusyon o runtime ay maaaring may halaga. Maaari ring mag-alok ang mga quantum algorithm ng mga bagong paraan para galugarin ang mga komplikadong solution space o pakinabangan ang estruktura sa mga partikular na klase ng problema. May matibay na teoretikal na motibasyon ang quantum machine learning para sa ilang problemang may classical na input, kabilang ang structured classification at pagproseso ng napakalalaking dataset. Gayunpaman, bukas pa ring tanong kung maisasalin ang mga resultang ito sa praktikal na advantage sa totoong classical na data. Inilalarawan ng partial differential equations ang maraming mahahalagang system sa agham, inhinyeriya, at pananalapi, at maaaring mapabuti ng mga quantum algorithm ang scaling ng ilang high-dimensional na simulation at malalaking linear-algebra na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In all three of these areas, however, the cost of preparing classical inputs, running the quantum computation, and extracting a useful classical answer can outweigh the benefit of the quantum step. We'll keep these practical challenges in mind as we explore how quantum methods are applied in each area.\n"
msgstr "Sa lahat ng tatlong larangang ito, gayunpaman, maaaring mas malaki ang gastos sa paghahanda ng classical na input, pagpapatakbo ng quantum computation, at pagkuha ng kapaki-pakinabang na classical na sagot kaysa sa benepisyo ng quantum na hakbang. Isasaisip natin ang mga praktikal na hamong ito habang tinutuklas natin kung paano inilalapat ang mga quantum na pamamaraan sa bawat larangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Near-term quantum utility and advantage {#near-term-quantum-utility-and-advantage}"
msgstr "Near-term na quantum utility at advantage {#near-term-quantum-utility-and-advantage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course isn't specifically about quantum advantage, but a discussion of quantum advantage is unavoidable. The fundamental motivation behind quantum applications is to use quantum resources to extend what classical computers can do alone: to produce more accurate results, reach solutions faster, or solve problems that are otherwise inaccessible. The following related terms help us talk clearly about the progress we see:\n"
msgstr "Hindi partikular na tungkol sa quantum advantage ang kursong ito, pero hindi maiiwasang pag-usapan ito. Ang pangunahing motibasyon sa likod ng mga quantum na aplikasyon ay gamitin ang mga quantum resource para palawakin ang kayang gawin ng mga classical computer nang mag-isa: makabuo ng mas tumpak na resulta, makarating sa mga solusyon nang mas mabilis, o lutasin ang mga problemang hindi maabot kung hindi. Ang mga sumusunod na magkakaugnay na termino ay tumutulong sa atin na malinaw na talakayin ang progresong nakikita natin:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum speedup:** As problem size increases, the time required by a quantum method scales more favorably than that of the best relevant classical method for the same task.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum speedup:** Habang lumalaki ang problema, mas paborable ang pag-scale ng oras na kailangan ng isang quantum na pamamaraan kumpara sa pinakamahusay na kaugnay na classical na pamamaraan para sa parehong gawain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum advantage:** A quantum-enabled computation outperforms the best relevant classical approaches on a well-defined task and meaningful metric. Rather than a single, permanent milestone, quantum advantage is an evolving frontier that shifts as both quantum and classical methods improve.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum advantage:** Nahihigitan ng isang quantum-enabled na computation ang pinakamahusay na kaugnay na classical na pamamaraan sa isang malinaw na tinukoy na gawain at makabuluhang metric. Sa halip na isang solong at permanenteng milestone, ang quantum advantage ay isang umuunlad na hangganan na gumagalaw habang bumubuti ang parehong quantum at classical na pamamaraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum utility:** A quantum computation contributes to a useful scientific or technical result. It operates at a scale, depth, and accuracy beyond practical brute-force classical simulation, without necessarily outperforming the best classical method.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum utility:** Nag-aambag ang isang quantum computation sa isang kapaki-pakinabang na siyentipiko o teknikal na resulta. Gumagana ito sa sukat, lalim, at katumpakang lampas sa praktikal na brute-force na classical simulation, nang hindi kinakailangang higitan ang pinakamahusay na classical na pamamaraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Near-term algorithm:** An algorithm designed for current quantum processors, using limited circuit depths and often relying on classical post-processing and error mitigation rather than full quantum error correction.\n"
msgstr "**Near-term algorithm:** Isang algorithm na dinisenyo para sa kasalukuyang mga quantum processor, na gumagamit ng limitadong circuit depth at madalas na umaasa sa classical post-processing at error mitigation sa halip na ganap na quantum error correction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fault-tolerant quantum computing:** In the future, quantum computing will use quantum error correction to protect logical qubits throughout a computation. When physical error rates are below the fault-tolerance threshold, additional error-correction resources can suppress logical errors to the level that long, reliable computations require. Fault tolerance makes much deeper algorithms possible, including large-scale implementations of Shor's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "**Fault-tolerant quantum computing:** Sa hinaharap, gagamit ang quantum computing ng quantum error correction para protektahan ang mga logical qubit sa buong computation. Kapag mas mababa ang mga physical error rate kaysa sa fault-tolerance threshold, kayang pigilan ng karagdagang resource sa error-correction ang mga logical error hanggang sa antas na kailangan ng mahahaba at maaasahang computation. Ginagawang posible ng fault tolerance ang mas malalalim na algorithm, kabilang ang malakihang implementasyon ng algorithm ni Shor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Early fault tolerance:** Fault tolerance means that errors are suppressed, not eliminated entirely. In early fault-tolerant systems, residual logical errors must still be accounted for, and the depth of reliable circuits remains limited.\n"
msgstr "**Early fault tolerance:** Ang ibig sabihin ng fault tolerance ay napipigilan ang mga error, hindi lubusang naaalis. Sa mga maagang fault-tolerant na system, kailangan pa ring isaalang-alang ang natitirang logical error, at limitado pa rin ang lalim ng mga maaasahang circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Heuristic algorithm:** A method designed to find a good solution in practice without guaranteeing the optimal answer or a particular runtime.\n"
msgstr "**Heuristic algorithm:** Isang pamamaraang dinisenyo para makahanap ng mahusay na solusyon sa praktika nang hindi ginagarantiya ang pinakamainam na sagot o isang partikular na runtime.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "A brief foundation in complexity theory {#a-brief-foundation-in-complexity-theory}"
msgstr "Maikling pundasyon sa complexity theory {#a-brief-foundation-in-complexity-theory}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In some application areas, we have a strong theoretical reason to expect that a quantum computer might have an advantage. To understand where that confidence comes from, we need a little vocabulary from complexity theory.\n"
msgstr "Sa ilang larangan ng aplikasyon, mayroon tayong matibay na teoretikal na dahilan para asahang maaaring magkaroon ng advantage ang isang quantum computer. Para maunawaan kung saan nanggagaling ang kumpiyansang ito, kailangan natin ng kaunting bokabularyo mula sa complexity theory.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complexity theory studies how the resources needed to solve a problem grow as the problem gets bigger. It gives us a useful map of where a quantum speedup might be possible. A few terms are especially important for this course:\n"
msgstr "Pinag-aaralan ng complexity theory kung paano lumalaki ang mga resource na kailangan para lutasin ang isang problema habang lumalaki ang problema. Nagbibigay ito sa atin ng kapaki-pakinabang na mapa kung saan maaaring posible ang quantum speedup. Ilang termino ang lalong mahalaga sa kursong ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**P:** Problems that a classical computer can solve efficiently, meaning that the required resources grow polynomially with the size of the problem.\n"
msgstr "**P:** Mga problemang kayang lutasin nang mahusay ng isang classical computer, ibig sabihin ay polynomial ang paglaki ng mga kinakailangang resource kaugnay ng laki ng problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NP:** Problems for which you can efficiently check a proposed solution, even if finding that solution might be very difficult.\n"
msgstr "**NP:** Mga problemang kayang suriin nang mahusay ang isang iminungkahing solusyon, kahit na maaaring napakahirap hanapin ang solusyong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NP-hard:** Problems that are at least as hard as every problem in NP. An NP-hard problem does not necessarily belong to NP. Many optimization problems are NP-hard.\n"
msgstr "**NP-hard:** Mga problemang kasing-hirap man lang ng bawat problema sa NP. Ang isang NP-hard na problema ay hindi kinakailangang kabilang sa NP. Maraming optimization problem ang NP-hard.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NP-complete:** Problems that are both NP-hard and in NP. These are the hardest decision problems within NP.\n"
msgstr "**NP-complete:** Mga problemang parehong NP-hard at nasa NP. Ito ang pinakamahihirap na decision problem sa loob ng NP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**BQP:** Problems that a quantum computer can solve efficiently with a bounded probability of error.\n"
msgstr "**BQP:** Mga problemang kayang lutasin nang mahusay ng isang quantum computer na may bounded na probabilidad ng error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some relationships among these categories are known. P is contained in both NP and BQP because a problem that can be solved efficiently on a classical computer can also be checked classically and solved on a quantum computer. Other relationships remain open. We don't know whether P equals NP or whether NP is contained in BQP. However, researchers generally believe that P is smaller than both NP and BQP, and that quantum computers cannot efficiently solve every NP-complete problem. In plain terms, a quantum computer is not a magic box that instantly solves every hard problem.\n"
msgstr "May ilang kilalang ugnayan sa pagitan ng mga kategoryang ito. Nasa loob ng parehong NP at BQP ang P dahil ang problemang kayang lutasin nang mahusay sa isang classical computer ay kaya ring suriin nang classical at lutasin sa isang quantum computer. May iba pang ugnayang bukas pa rin. Hindi natin alam kung ang P ay katumbas ng NP o kung ang NP ay nasa loob ng BQP. Gayunpaman, karaniwang naniniwala ang mga mananaliksik na mas maliit ang P kaysa sa parehong NP at BQP, at na hindi kayang lutasin nang mahusay ng mga quantum computer ang bawat NP-complete na problema. Sa simpleng salita, ang isang quantum computer ay hindi mahiwagang kahon na agad na lumulutas ng bawat mahirap na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The strongest complexity-based arguments for quantum computing apply to particular kinds of problems. Shor's algorithm scales dramatically better than the best-known classical algorithms for factoring and discrete logarithms, although factoring has not been proven to be outside P. General quantum simulation also has a strong theoretical foundation. Some quantum-simulation problems are BQP-complete, meaning that efficiently solving them classically would amount to efficiently simulating any quantum computation. Such an efficient classical simulation is highly implausible, which is one reason that quantum Hamiltonian simulation is considered such a promising application area.\n"
msgstr "Ang pinakamatitibay na argumentong nakabatay sa complexity para sa quantum computing ay para sa mga partikular na uri ng problema. Mas mahusay nang husto ang pag-scale ng algorithm ni Shor kaysa sa pinakakilalang classical na algorithm para sa factoring at discrete logarithm, bagaman hindi pa napatunayang nasa labas ng P ang factoring. May matibay ding teoretikal na pundasyon ang pangkalahatang quantum simulation. Ang ilang quantum-simulation na problema ay BQP-complete, ibig sabihin ang mahusay na paglutas sa mga ito nang classical ay katumbas ng mahusay na pag-simulate sa anumang quantum computation. Lubhang malabong mangyari ang ganoong mahusay na classical simulation, na isa sa mga dahilan kung bakit itinuturing na napakapromising na larangan ng aplikasyon ang quantum Hamiltonian simulation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some high-dimensional PDEs can be reduced to BQP-complete linear-system problems, giving us a strong reason to expect a quantum speedup when inputs and outputs can be handled efficiently. QML has similar examples: some tasks involving quantum data are BQP-complete, and some quantum models can generate samples that are difficult to reproduce classically.\n"
msgstr "Ang ilang high-dimensional na PDE ay maaaring gawing BQP-complete na linear-system na problema, na nagbibigay sa atin ng matibay na dahilan para asahan ang quantum speedup kapag mahusay na mahahawakan ang mga input at output. May katulad na mga halimbawa ang QML: ang ilang gawaing may kinalaman sa quantum data ay BQP-complete, at ang ilang quantum model ay kayang bumuo ng mga sample na mahirap gayahin nang classical.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The case is less straightforward for optimization. Quantum computers are not expected to solve arbitrary NP-hard problems efficiently, but they might still help with structured problems, particular instances, or specific steps in an optimization workflow. Grover's algorithm, for example, gives a quadratic speedup for unstructured search. That is a meaningful improvement, even though the square root of an astronomically large search space can still be astronomical.\n"
msgstr "Hindi gaanong tuwiran ang kaso para sa optimization. Hindi inaasahang malulutas nang mahusay ng mga quantum computer ang mga arbitraryong NP-hard na problema, pero maaari pa rin silang makatulong sa mga structured na problema, partikular na instance, o tiyak na hakbang sa isang optimization workflow. Halimbawa, nagbibigay ang algorithm ni Grover ng quadratic speedup para sa unstructured search. Makabuluhang pagbuti iyon, kahit na ang square root ng isang napakalaking search space ay maaari pa ring maging napakalaki.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "From complexity theory to practical evidence {#from-complexity-theory-to-practical-evidence}"
msgstr "Mula sa complexity theory tungo sa praktikal na ebidensya {#from-complexity-theory-to-practical-evidence}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complexity theory can tell us where a quantum speedup might be possible, but it usually can't tell us how a method performs on a particular problem or a particular quantum computer. Many of the methods used on current hardware are heuristic. They are designed to find good answers in practice, but they do not guarantee the best possible answer or a particular runtime.\n"
msgstr "Masasabi sa atin ng complexity theory kung saan maaaring posible ang quantum speedup, pero kadalasan ay hindi nito masasabi kung paano gumaganap ang isang pamamaraan sa isang partikular na problema o partikular na quantum computer. Marami sa mga pamamaraang ginagamit sa kasalukuyang hardware ay heuristic. Dinisenyo ang mga ito para makahanap ng mahusay na sagot sa praktika, pero hindi nila ginagarantiya ang pinakamainam na sagot o isang partikular na runtime.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heuristics are not unique to quantum computing, and calling a method heuristic does not mean that it is unreliable or unscientific. Classical optimization, machine learning, and computational chemistry all rely heavily on heuristics when an exact solution would be too expensive. A quantum heuristic might offer a new way to explore a solution space, prepare useful states, or identify promising candidates. Whether it works well is an empirical question: we have to run it and measure the result.\n"
msgstr "Hindi natatangi sa quantum computing ang mga heuristic, at ang pagtawag sa isang pamamaraan na heuristic ay hindi nangangahulugang hindi ito maaasahan o hindi siyentipiko. Malaki ang pag-asa ng classical optimization, machine learning, at computational chemistry sa mga heuristic kapag masyadong magastos ang eksaktong solusyon. Maaaring mag-alok ang isang quantum heuristic ng bagong paraan para galugarin ang solution space, maghanda ng mga kapaki-pakinabang na state, o tukuyin ang mga promising na kandidato. Isang empirikal na tanong kung gumagana ito nang mahusay: kailangan natin itong patakbuhin at sukatin ang resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because heuristics don't come with performance guarantees, we evaluate them using a clear success metric, strong classical baselines, and tests across different problem sizes. This helps us see where a method works well and how its performance changes as the problem scales.\n"
msgstr "Dahil walang kasamang garantiya sa performance ang mga heuristic, sinusuri natin ang mga ito gamit ang malinaw na success metric, matitibay na classical baseline, at mga test sa iba't ibang laki ng problema. Nakakatulong ito para makita natin kung saan mahusay gumagana ang isang pamamaraan at kung paano nagbabago ang performance nito habang lumalaki ang problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Application areas and course case studies {#application-areas-and-course-case-studies}"
msgstr "Mga larangan ng aplikasyon at mga case study ng kurso {#application-areas-and-course-case-studies}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We organize the course around four broad application areas. They don't cover every possible use of a quantum computer, but they give us a useful way to compare where the strongest arguments lie and where the open questions are.\n"
msgstr "Inaayos natin ang kurso sa paligid ng apat na malawak na larangan ng aplikasyon. Hindi nila sinasaklaw ang bawat posibleng gamit ng isang quantum computer, pero nagbibigay sila sa atin ng kapaki-pakinabang na paraan para ihambing kung saan nakatayo ang pinakamatitibay na argumento at kung nasaan ang mga bukas na tanong.\n"

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation {#hamiltonian-simulation}"
msgstr "Simulasyon ng Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation includes estimating energies, studying chemical and material properties, and modeling how quantum systems change over time. It reaches across chemistry, materials science, condensed-matter physics, and high-energy and nuclear physics. Our case studies examine a strongly correlated iron-sulfur model using sample-based quantum diagonalization and simulate hadron dynamics using a symmetry-aware lattice representation. These are two examples from a much larger field, which also includes reaction mechanisms, magnetic materials, and other many-body dynamics.\n"
msgstr "Kasama sa Hamiltonian simulation ang pagtantya ng mga energy, pag-aaral ng mga katangiang kemikal at ng materyales, at pagmomodelo kung paano nagbabago sa paglipas ng panahon ang mga quantum system. Sumasaklaw ito sa chemistry, materials science, condensed-matter physics, at high-energy at nuclear physics. Sinusuri ng ating mga case study ang isang strongly correlated na iron-sulfur model gamit ang sample-based quantum diagonalization at sini-simulate ang dynamics ng hadron gamit ang symmetry-aware na lattice representation. Dalawa lang ito sa maraming halimbawa mula sa mas malaking larangan, na kinabibilangan din ng mga reaction mechanism, magnetic na materyales, at iba pang many-body dynamics.\n"

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization {#optimization}"
msgstr "Optimisasyon {#optimization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization appears everywhere from finance and logistics to scheduling and energy systems. It is also an area in which advantage is difficult to establish, because classical solvers are extremely capable and quantum mappings can add costly overhead. Our case study uses portfolio selection to explore how an optimization problem is represented, run, and benchmarked without assuming that a quantum computer automatically finds the exact optimum.\n"
msgstr "Lumilitaw ang optimization saanman mula sa pananalapi at logistics hanggang sa scheduling at mga energy system. Isa rin itong larangan kung saan mahirap itatag ang advantage, dahil napakahusay ng mga classical solver at maaaring magdagdag ng magastos na overhead ang mga quantum mapping. Gumagamit ang ating case study ng portfolio selection para tuklasin kung paano nirerepresenta, pinapatakbo, at bina-benchmark ang isang optimization problem nang hindi ina-assume na awtomatikong mahahanap ng quantum computer ang eksaktong optimum.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum machine learning {#quantum-machine-learning}"
msgstr "Quantum machine learning {#quantum-machine-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum machine learning asks whether quantum circuits or quantum data can improve a learning task. Important questions include data encoding, training cost, generalization, and comparison with strong classical models.\n"
msgstr "Tinatanong ng quantum machine learning kung mapapabuti ng mga quantum circuit o quantum data ang isang gawain sa pagkatuto. Kabilang sa mahahalagang tanong ang data encoding, gastos sa training, generalization, at paghahambing sa matitibay na classical model.\n"

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial differential equations {#partial-differential-equations}"
msgstr "Mga partial differential equation {#partial-differential-equations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial differential equations describe systems such as fluids, heat, and waves. Quantum algorithms might accelerate parts of some PDE workflows, but data preparation and extracting a useful classical answer can be major costs. The specific case study is still being developed.\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng partial differential equations ang mga system tulad ng mga fluid, init, at alon. Maaaring pabilisin ng mga quantum algorithm ang mga bahagi ng ilang PDE workflow, pero maaaring malaking gastos ang paghahanda ng data at pagkuha ng kapaki-pakinabang na classical na sagot. Binubuo pa ang partikular na case study.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the lessons that follow, we'll ask the same basic questions in each area: What is the problem, why might quantum computing help, what are the limitations, and what does the evidence actually show? We'll start with Hamiltonian simulation, where the problem itself is quantum.\n"
msgstr "Sa mga susunod na lesson, itatanong natin ang parehong pangunahing mga tanong sa bawat larangan: Ano ang problema, bakit maaaring makatulong ang quantum computing, ano ang mga limitasyon, at ano talaga ang ipinapakita ng ebidensya? Magsisimula tayo sa Hamiltonian simulation, kung saan quantum na mismo ang problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Konklusyon {#conclusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We've covered a lot of ground, but the main idea is simple: quantum computers are specialized tools, and their value depends on using the right quantum method for the right problem or piece of a larger problem. Hamiltonian simulation has the clearest theoretical foundation, optimization has a mature set of heuristic methods and benchmarks, and QML and PDEs offer promising directions that are still developing.\n"
msgstr "Marami na tayong nasaklaw, pero simple ang pangunahing ideya: ang mga quantum computer ay mga espesyalisadong tool, at nakasalalay ang halaga nila sa paggamit ng tamang quantum na pamamaraan para sa tamang problema o bahagi ng mas malaking problema. Ang Hamiltonian simulation ang may pinakamalinaw na teoretikal na pundasyon, ang optimization ay may mature na hanay ng mga heuristic na pamamaraan at benchmark, at ang QML at PDEs ay nag-aalok ng mga promising na direksyong patuloy pang umuunlad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the lessons that follow, we'll move from this broad overview to hands-on examples. For each application, we'll ask what problem we're trying to solve, what role the quantum computer plays, how the result is interpreted, and what we can learn from it. The goal is to build your intuition for where quantum computing might help and what it takes to turn a promising idea into a real computation.\n"
msgstr "Sa mga susunod na lesson, lilipat tayo mula sa malawak na pangkalahatang-ideyang ito tungo sa mga hands-on na halimbawa. Para sa bawat aplikasyon, itatanong natin kung anong problema ang sinusubukan nating lutasin, anong papel ang ginagampanan ng quantum computer, paano binibigyang-kahulugan ang resulta, at ano ang matututunan natin mula rito. Layunin nitong buuin ang iyong intuwisyon kung saan maaaring makatulong ang quantum computing at kung ano ang kailangan para gawing totoong computation ang isang promising na ideya.\n"
